The '''Lothal cliff dwelling''' was located in the southern hemisphere of the [[planet]] [[Lothal]]. It served as a base for the [[Lothal resistance group]] and the [[Spectres]] during the [[Early rebellion against the Galactic Empire|early rebellion]] against the [[Galactic Empire]] in [[1 BBY]]. The cliff dwelling was also the site of a skirmish between the rebels and Imperial [[Governor]] [[Arihnda Pryce]]'s forces prior to the [[Liberation of Lothal]].

==Description==
The Lothal cliff dwelling<ref name="Behind-the-Scenes Gallery">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/kindred-behind-the-scenes-gallery|text="Kindred" Behind-the-Scenes Gallery}} {{C|Slide 5}}</ref> was located in the southern hemisphere of the [[planet]] [[Lothal]]. The dwelling consisted of a network of [[cave]]s that appeared to have been built by the ancient people of the planet, and contained cave [[painting]]s depicting people and [[Loth-wolf|Loth-wolves]]. The people in the paintings were shown descending from space and appeared to be [[Jedi]].<ref name="Kindred" />

==History==
In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Kindred date">{{RebelsDate|407}}</ref> the [[Spectres|rebels]] [[Ezra Bridger]], [[Sabine Wren]], [[Kanan Jarrus]], and [[Ryder Azadi]] were brought there from a [[Loth-wolf den|cave]] in the northern hemisphere by three wolves while fleeing an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[assassin]]. The structure reminded [[Ezra Bridger]] and Jarrus, both Jedi, of the [[Lothal Jedi Temple]].<ref name="Kindred" /> After the discovery, the [[Lothal resistance group]] decided to use the dwelling as a base.<ref name="Crawler Commandeers" />

Following [[General]] [[Hera Syndulla]]'s [[Attack on Lothal|failed attack]] on the [[Imperial Armory Complex]], the Spectres and Lothal resistance retreated to the base. The Spectres under the leadership of Ezra assembled three [[Loth-bat glider]]s, which they used to infiltrate the [[Imperial Complex (Lothal)|Imperial Complex]] in [[Capital City]].<ref name="Jedi Night">{{Rebels|Jedi Night}}</ref> Following the death of Kanan, Hera mourned for her lover insider the caves of the cliff dwelling. Ryder, [[Mart Mattin]], and [[Jai Kell]] also listened to a [[propaganda]] broadcast by [[Alton Kastle]] claiming that the rebellion on Lothal was a lost cause. However, Sabine and [[Garazeb Orrelios]] subsequently discovered that the destruction of the [[Lothal City fuel depot]] had damaged the Imperial Armory Complex.<ref name="DUME">{{Rebels|DUME}}</ref>

After discussing their plans, the Spectres departed from the cliff dwelling on a [[Mission to the Lothal Jedi Temple|mission]] to save the [[Lothal Jedi Temple]].<ref name="Wolves and a Door">{{Rebels|Wolves and a Door}}</ref> The Lothal cliff dwelling was later the site of a skirmish between the Lothal rebels and [[Governor]] [[Arihnda Pryce]]'s forces. However, this was a ruse by Ezra and Ryder to lure Governor Pryce into a trap as part of their plan to expel the Galactic Empire from [[Capital City]]. Despite significant casualties, Pryce's forces were defeated with the help of Hera's reinforcements and a pack of loth-wolves. As a result, the rebels managed to capture Pryce and several [[stormtrooper]]s.<ref name="A Fool's Hope">{{Rebels|A Fool's Hope}}</ref>

Following Pryce's capture, the rebels departed on two captured [[LAAT/le patrol gunship|patrol transports]] to infiltrate the Imperial Complex in Capital City. The [[Noghri]] assassin [[Rukh]] stole a third patrol transport and managed to alert [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]] about the rebels' plans to seize the Imperial Complex. In response, [[Wolffe]], Mart, and [[Cikatro Vizago]] departed on the ''[[Ghost]]'' on a secret mission to contact a pod of [[purrgil]] as part of Ezra's back-up plan.<ref name="Family Reunion">{{Rebels|Family Reunion &ndash; and Farewell}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Lothal cliff dwelling first appeared in the ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'' [[Star Wars Rebels Season Four|Season Four]] episode "[[Kindred]]," which premiered on [[November 6]], [[2017]]. It was first identified as the "cliff dwelling" in the episode's Behind the Scenes gallery on the official Star Wars website [[StarWars.com]].<ref name="Behind-the-Scenes Gallery" /> The cliff dwelling also appeared in several Season Four episodes including the season finale "[[Family Reunion – and Farewell]]," which premiered on [[March 5]], [[2018]].

